WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:10.160
Dealing with written content online is more complex and more demanding than ever.

2
00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:16.855
Disinformation, derivative content and the sheer volume of information make it

3
00:00:16.855 --> 00:00:18.775
hard to keep track.

4
00:00:18.855 --> 00:00:22.775
Fake news and deliberate manipulation make researching a text far harder.

5
00:00:24.055 --> 00:00:27.975
Doppelcheck helps readers with that challenge, in the form of a browser

6
00:00:27.975 --> 00:00:28.535
extension.

7
00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:33.130
First, the software extracts the central claims of a text.

8
00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:38.250
It then checks them against further sources that the reader considers trustworthy.

9
00:00:45.065 --> 00:00:49.385
Using a simple colour code, Doppelcheck shows whether there is agreement

10
00:00:49.385 --> 00:00:53.305
or contradiction between the text being examined and those further sources.

11
00:00:53.465 --> 00:00:57.910
Unlike conventional fact-checkers, Doppelcheck works entirely locally on

12
00:00:57.910 --> 00:00:59.110
your own machine.

13
00:00:59.110 --> 00:01:03.030
Your data stays safe, and you decide for yourself which sources are

14
00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:04.150
trustworthy to you.
